From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:44:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Reserve the soft pagezero of an entitled macOS arm64
 loader.

With com.apple.developer.cross-architecture-support the 4GB hard pagezero
becomes one hard page plus a prot 0/0 reservation that MAP_FIXED may replace.
Register it as a reserved area, like the x86_64 zerofill reserve, so
map_fixed_area can place KUSER_SHARED_DATA at 0x7ffe0000.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 9d3a0f22..994a8dee 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3279,6 +3279,27 @@ void virtual_init(void)
         reserve_area( (void *)0x7f000000, (void *)0x7fff0000 );
     }
 
+#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__aarch64__)
+    {
+        /* With com.apple.developer.cross-architecture-support the 4GB hard pagezero becomes one
+         * hard page plus a soft prot 0/0 reservation that MAP_FIXED may replace: treat it like
+         * the x86_64 zerofill reserve, so nothing else lands in the low 4GB (a mem area, since Wine's mem_areas
+         * replaced the reserved list). */
+        mach_vm_address_t addr = 0;
+        mach_vm_size_t size;
+        vm_region_basic_info_data_64_t info;
+        mach_msg_type_number_t count = VM_REGION_BASIC_INFO_COUNT_64;
+        mach_port_t obj;
+
+        if (!mach_vm_region( mach_task_self(), &addr, &size, VM_REGION_BASIC_INFO_64,
+                             (vm_region_info_t)&info, &count, &obj ))
+        {
+            TRACE( "lowest region %#llx-%#llx prot %d/%d\n", addr, addr + size, info.protection, info.max_protection );
+            if (addr && addr < 0x100000000 && !info.max_protection) set_mem_area_state( (void *)addr, size, AREA_RESERVED );
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (is_win64) /* top-down area */
     {
         void *start = (void *)0x7ff000000000;
